        {
          "id": "528fd217-1e4d-3f44-9196-420790cc21da",
          "content": {
            "id": "528fd217-1e4d-3f44-9196-420790cc21da",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "SoftBank to buy ABB's robot business for $5.4 billion",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: SoftBank Group has agreed to buy the robotics business of Swiss engineering group ABB in a $5.4 billion deal.</p><p>The Japanese investor is forging\u00a0ahead with a strategy to fuse robotics and artificial intelligence.</p><p>The acquisition is the latest by Softbank as it seeks to become a core player in the development of AI.</p><p>Its recent investments in the sector include Berkshire Grey and AutoStore.</p><p>It also led a $40 billion funding round in ChatGPT-maker OpenAI.</p><p>The deal means ABB has abandoned its original decision to spin off and separately list the industrial automation business.</p><p>It follows years of struggling sales and falling profitability for the robots business.</p><p>ABB's robotics division employs 7,000 people.</p><p>And generated sales of $2.3 billion last year - around 7% of ABB's total revenues.</p><p>Its shares opened 2% higher in Zurich after the sale announcement.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: SoftBank Group has agreed to buy the robotics business of Swiss engineering group ABB in a $5.4 billion deal.</p><p>The Japanese investor is forging&nbsp;ahead with a strategy to fuse robotics and artificial intelligence.</p><p>The acquisition is the latest by Softbank as it seeks to become a core player in the development of AI.</p><p>Its recent investments in the sector include Berkshire Grey and AutoStore.</p><p>It also led a $40 billion funding round in ChatGPT-maker OpenAI.</p><p>The deal means ABB has abandoned its original decision to spin off and separately list the industrial automation business.</p><p>It follows years of struggling sales and falling profitability for the robots business.</p><p>ABB's robotics division employs 7,000 people.</p><p>And generated sales of $2.3 billion last year - around 7% of ABB's total revenues.</p><p>Its shares opened 2% higher in Zurich after the sale announcement.</p></body>",
